(reports/'BNT_M6_P1_Identity_Lifecycle_Report.md').write_text('# Identity lifecycle validation\n\nHome driver acquisition failure is reproduced in the original packaged M6 HTML and corrected in P1. Offered identity, ancestry, name, source provenance and visual sex are copied exactly; native personality/contract/price remain authoritative. Ordinary Home and Regional driver hires, reload, exact charges and unchanged frozen registration are covered separately.\n\nThe generated matrix covers all13 ancestries×male/female, using an explicitly seeded epoch1 renewal per career, followed by protected native hiring, duplicate retries and cold validation. It is not described as26 ordinary UI hires. Specialist ancestry/sex follows immutable context across acquisition; chariot/beast/equipment/staff acquisition and sale/termination test orphan cleanup. Contract expiry retains the owned identity until explicit release; renewals do not mint new assets. Destroyed chariots are not silently deleted.\n\nNational rival sex is keyed by immutable driver member ID; local members follow the active championship, and Den local keys follow committed event/entrant identities. Persistent Den members reuse national identity. Staff preserves existing authored canonical ancestry/sex; only absent values use a separate national sampling/hash domain. Existing mechanical profiles, market sequences and Owner sex are unchanged. Cold-load validation rejects foreign keys, unsupported versions and contradictory values; failed writes do not publish partial maps.\n\nThe emergency route is now corrected under the explicit owner policy: native recruitment provenance gates neutral1.00 affinity with all nine species; portrait ancestry/sex are deterministic and cosmetic. Native costs,40 attributes, wage20 and one-cycle employment remain. Protected birth evidence survives acknowledgment eviction and release. Nine-species native participation, ordinary packaged original-stock execution, real-IDB backup/restore, expiry and counter-tests are documented separately.\n')
(reports/'BNT_M6_P1_Gameplay_and_Economic_Integrity.md').write_text('# Gameplay and economic integrity\n\nNative official publication, final settlement, market quotes, contract terms, protected financial anchors, M6 high-water marks and reward IDs remain unchanged. Native full championships, Run selection, terminal selection, archive/renewal and cold retry were executed. Source-to-domain guards and atomic storage faults remain enabled.\n\nActual participated wagers resolve only after official classification and credit at final settlement. Three consecutive native Den events settle once; failed writes and duplicate requests cannot apply another payout. Spectator racing leaves stable condition, world, championships, payroll and Legacy unchanged. Named last results are an optional bounded presentation summary from the trusted native completion capability.\n\nTies/dead heats, DNF, void/no-winner, withdrawal, caps, floor rounding, stale requests and corruption are tested at explicit boundaries, not falsely claimed as all organically observed. No Bannerfall trophy is fabricated; Sundaran registration uses seven native national-victory facts and the existing Iron Gauntlet economic context. Local/Prestige qualification and market grades use existing authority.\n\nAll29 Run options (21base+8abilities), eight Legacy upgrades and six Signs were reviewed against their source hooks. Stat/cap, healing/injury, repair/wear, immediate Gold, discount and one-charge semantics remain unchanged. Ability text is versioned with new-run correction; existing v2 offers reconstruct exactly. No general balancing or new reward effect was introduced.\n\nEmergency replacement uses the owner-approved, native-proven neutral exception; actual native two-event final settlement preserves20-Gold wage and one-cycle expiry. No apparent restart issue was concealed: the accepted unfinished-race restart model permits different player decisions, while fixed spectator setup/stake and official result IDs prevent new stakes or duplicated settlement. Broad long-term gambling calibration remains provisional.\n')
pt='# Persistence and performance\n\nNo persistence backend, per-record limit, financial history rule or durable acknowledgment guarantee was replaced. Native ordinary playback retains zero durable writes; completed results and consequential decisions use existing commits. Visual metadata remains bounded by live scope, and last Den results retain at most8named rows.\n\n'
pt+=f"Eight completed native championships retain one current record; the largest seven-event/eight-entrant fixture retained {ret.get('logicalBytes')} bytes while unresolved and compacted to {ret.get('compactBytes')} bytes. Real IndexedDB, Worker, previous generation, complete backup and restore were executed. Backup size {ret.get('backupBytes')} bytes. Concurrent-load measurements: backup {ret.get('backupMs')}ms, restore {ret.get('restoreMs')}ms, validation {ret.get('validationMs')}ms, longest main-thread task {ret.get('longestMainThreadMs')}ms, observed JS heap {ret.get('memory',{}).get('used')} bytes. These show a significant remaining responsiveness limitation, not a passing50/100ms target. No larger architecture redesign was undertaken.\n\n"
